---
import LegalPage from '../../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, OPERATOR_NAME, SITE_DOMAIN, SITE_NAME } from '../../lib/legal';

const title = `Privacy Policy | ${SITE_NAME}`;
const description =
    'How Canadian Credit Card Finder handles your information: no accounts, Google Analytics 4, Google AdSense cookies, ad personalization choices, and your rights under PIPEDA.';
---

<LegalPage title={title} heading="Privacy Policy" description={description} breadcrumb="Privacy Policy">
    <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains what information is collected when you visit {SITE_NAME} at{' '}
        <a href="https://canadiancreditcardfinder.com/">{SITE_DOMAIN}</a> (the "site"), how it is used, and the
        choices you have. The site is run by {OPERATOR_NAME} ("we", "us", "our") in Canada, and we aim to follow
        Canada's <em>Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act</em> (PIPEDA).
    </p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>The site is an informational credit card comparison tool. There are no user accounts, sign-ups, or forms that ask for your name, address, or financial details.</li>
        <li>We use Google Analytics 4 to understand how the site is used, and Google AdSense to show ads. Both use cookies or similar technologies.</li>
        <li>Some links to card issuers are affiliate links. We may earn a commission if you apply through them.</li>
        <li>We do not sell your personal information.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <h3>Information you give us</h3>
    <p>
        We don't ask you to create an account or submit personal information to use the site. If you choose to
        email us, we will receive your email address and whatever you include in your message, and we use it
        only to reply to you.
    </p>
    <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
    <p>
        Like most websites, our hosting provider and the third-party services described below automatically
        receive standard technical information when you visit, such as your IP address, browser type, device
        type, operating system, referring page, the pages you view, and the date and time of your visit.
    </p>
    <h3>Information stored in your browser</h3>
    <p>
        Some features, such as the card comparison list, save your selections in your own browser's local
        storage so they're still there when you come back. This data stays on your device; we don't receive it.
        You can clear it at any time by clearing your browser's site data.
    </p>

    <h2>Google Analytics 4</h2>
    <p>
        We use Google Analytics 4, a web analytics service provided by Google, to see aggregate information
        such as how many people visit, which pages are popular, and how visitors find the site. Google Analytics
        uses cookies and similar technologies to collect this information. We use these reports to improve the
        site; we don't use them to identify individual visitors.
    </p>
    <p>
        You can opt out of Google Analytics on all websites by installing the{' '}
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Google AdSense and advertising cookies</h2>
    <p>
        We use Google AdSense to display ads. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads
        based on your prior visits to this site and other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables
        it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visits to this site and/or other sites on the
        internet.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            You can learn more about how Google uses information from sites that use its services at{' '}
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
            You can opt out of personalized advertising from Google by visiting{' '}
            <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings (adssettings.google.com)</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
            You can also opt out of some third-party vendors' use of cookies for personalized advertising at{' '}
            <a href="https://youradchoices.ca/" rel="noopener">youradchoices.ca</a> (Digital Advertising Alliance of Canada) or{' '}
            <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="noopener">aboutads.info</a>.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        If you opt out of personalized ads, you may still see ads, but they won't be based on your browsing
        history.
    </p>

    <h2>Managing cookies</h2>
    <p>
        Most browsers let you view, block, or delete cookies through their settings. If you block cookies, the
        site will still work, but analytics and ad personalization may not.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
        Some links on the site go to credit card issuers or partners and may include tracking that tells the
        partner you came from our site. If you click one of these links and apply for or are approved for a
        product, we may earn a commission. Once you leave our site, the partner's own privacy policy applies to
        any information you give them, including any card application.
    </p>

    <h2>How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>To operate, maintain, secure, and improve the site.</li>
        <li>To understand which pages and tools are useful, using aggregate analytics.</li>
        <li>To show ads that help keep the site free.</li>
        <li>To reply to you if you contact us.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sharing your information</h2>
    <p>
        We don't sell or rent your personal information. Information is shared only with the service providers
        that help run the site (such as our hosting provider, Google Analytics, and Google AdSense) as described
        above, or where required by law.
    </p>

    <h2>Where information is stored</h2>
    <p>
        Our service providers, including Google, may process and store information outside Canada, including in
        the United States. When that happens, the information is subject to the laws of those countries and
        may be accessible to their courts and authorities.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
        We keep information only as long as needed for the purposes above. Google Analytics data is kept
        according to the retention setting in our Google Analytics account, after which Google deletes it.
        Emails are kept only as long as needed to respond and keep a reasonable record.
    </p>

    <h2>Google API Services</h2>
    <p>
        Separately from this website, {OPERATOR_NAME} operates an internal YouTube tool that uses YouTube API
        Services to manage the operator's own YouTube channel. By using YouTube features, you agree to be bound
        by the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" rel="noopener">YouTube Terms of Service</a>. Information
        processed through YouTube API Services is also subject to the{' '}
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        This tool is used only by the site operator. No visitor data is accessed, collected, or stored through
        it, and website visitors do not interact with it.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
        The site is intended for adults researching credit products. It is not directed at children, and we do
        not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under the age of majority in their province.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights under PIPEDA</h2>
    <p>
        Under PIPEDA, you can ask to access the personal information we hold about you, ask us to correct it,
        or withdraw your consent to how we use it (subject to legal or contractual limits). Because we don't run
        accounts, we usually hold very little or no information that can identify you. To make a request, email
        us at the address below and we'll respond within 30 days.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you're not satisfied with our response, you can contact the{' '}
        <a href="https://www.priv.gc.ca/" rel="noopener">Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
        The site is served over HTTPS. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, but we use
        reasonable safeguards appropriate to the small amount of information involved.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we'll change the "Last updated" date at
        the top of this page.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
        Questions or requests about this policy? Email {OPERATOR_NAME} at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
    <p>See also our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
